  "rationale": "The subject has three obligations. All three are tested and asserted.\n\n1. **Extension selects a compiled-in language, and other files get the plain-text outline.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]` parses `note.unknown`. It asserts the `plain-text-structural-v1` fingerprint and a three-item outline (the root plus two nonblank lines).\n   - The same test parses `visible.rs`. It asserts the `rust-structural-v1` fingerprint.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[list_read_only_provider_supports_selected_language_parse_and_structural_search]` checks that `file.rs` parses with the Rust outline (`fn[provided]` resolves).\n\n2. **Text search uses regular expressions.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` searches `^n[e]{2}dle$`. It asserts 3 matches, which only regex semantics produce.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot]` runs the default text search. It asserts the match line and the excerpt with context.\n\n3. **Structural search uses the requested language's syntax capability, per `requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider.structural_search`.**\n   - The project-scope test runs structural search for `rust`, which returns only Rust matches. It runs `python`, which returns only `script.py`. It runs `plain-text`, which returns an unsupported-language error with the expected message. That error is the default-implementation behavior the cited requirement specifies.\n   - The list-read-only provider test covers a language/file mismatch (`python` over Rust text returns an empty, complete result). It also covers an unknown language (error), a malformed rule (error), and an explicit language overriding the extension.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[structural_search_uses_overridden_parses_their_snapshot_and_requested_scope]` covers use of the provider's parse and the requested scope.\n\nThe tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no unacknowledged gap.",
